    <h2 style="margin:56px 0 18px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Frequently asked questions
    </h2>

    <div style="border-top:2px solid #181818;">
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Do ceramides work for oily skin?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Yes. Oily skin can still have a weak barrier, and a light, non-comedogenic ceramide lotion supports it without feeling heavy.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/dry/pick-moisturizer" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>5</sup></a> Look for a gel-cream if creams feel rich.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Can I use a ceramide moisturizer with actives?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Yes, and it often helps. The moisturizer is the constant in the routine, and the active is the thing you introduce slowly. Add one active at a time, three or four days apart.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">How long does it take for the barrier to recover?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Many people notice skin feeling more comfortable within a couple of weeks of simpler care, though it varies from person to person. If dryness becomes painful or cracked, or does not improve, see a dermatologist.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/dry/pick-moisturizer" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>5</sup></a></p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Is a ceramide serum the same as a ceramide moisturizer?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">No. A serum adds hydration and may contain ceramides, but a moisturizer is the step that seals the routine. Use both if you like, and keep the moisturizer.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Do I need to avoid fragrance?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">On skin that is struggling, yes, it is worth avoiding. Dermatologists advise avoiding fragrance, alcohol and alpha hydroxy acids to help dry skin hold on to its natural oils.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-basics/dry/pick-moisturizer" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>5</sup></a></p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Can a moisturizer replace sunscreen?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">No. A moisturizer does not replace sunscreen, so keep a dedicated broad-spectrum sunscreen as your last morning step.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        References
    </h2>
